#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "What should be done when pacman refuses a package due to its inability to validate the signature, and how to manually verify Ditana's signing key yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "\"invalid or corrupted package (PGP signature)\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"Every package Ditana ships is signed, and pacman refuses to install one "
"whose signature it cannot check. That is the mechanism working. But it also "
"means a keyring that is out of date locks you out of the very updates that "
"would fix it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"You will see one of these, depending on whether the signing key is missing "
"from your keyring or present but not trusted:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"error: ditana-mirrorlist: key \"3EC223A811077C09\" is unknown\n"
":: Import PGP key 3EC223A811077C09? [Y/n]\n"
"error: 'ditana-mirrorlist-1.12-1-any.pkg.tar.zst': invalid or corrupted package (PGP signature)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"error: ditana-mirrorlist: signature from \"Stefan Zipproth <s.zipproth@ditana.org>\" is unknown trust\n"
"error: failed to commit transaction (invalid or corrupted package (PGP signature))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The repair"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid "For a Ditana package:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo pacman -Sy ditana-keyring\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"For an Arch package (the same problem, the same shape — this one is common "
"on systems that have been offline for months):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo pacman -Sy archlinux-keyring\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"This is the exception to the \"never `-Sy` a single package\" rule from "
"[Updating is not optional](/troubleshooting/updating/), and it is worth "
"understanding *why* it is safe rather than treating it as a magic "
"incantation. Only one package is in the transaction, so there is no partial "
"upgrade of a dependency graph. That package is small and contains no "
"executables. And its signature is verifiable with a key your installation "
"already has, so nothing is being trusted that was not trusted before — "
"installing it runs `pacman-key --populate`, which adds the current set of "
"Ditana keys to your keyring. Afterwards, run a **full** update as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"If you would rather do it by hand, this is exactly what the package's "
"install script runs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo pacman-key --populate ditana\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify the keys yourself"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid "Ditana packages are signed by this key:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"pub   rsa4096  3F80 54C3 FF75 5E55 44E6  8516 BC33 3E9A E877 D45A\n"
"uid   Stefan Zipproth <s.zipproth@ditana.org>\n"
"uid   Stefan Zipproth <support@ditana.org>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"It carries a dedicated signing subkey, and that subkey is what signs the "
"repository database and every package built since August 2026:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sub   rsa4096  068E EA2A 490B 0C63 AEAA  3BCD 3EC2 23A8 1107 7C09\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"The fingerprint you verify against stays the one above: a subkey can be "
"replaced without it changing. A keyring pre-dating `ditana-keyring 20260809` "
"does not know the subkey at all, which is exactly the situation the repair "
"above addresses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid "Check what your own system trusts with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"pacman-key --list-sigs ditana\n"
"gpg --show-keys --with-subkey-fingerprint /usr/share/pacman/keyrings/ditana.gpg\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"We deliberately do **not** offer a download-and-run repair script here. The "
"situation you are in is \"my signature verification is failing\"; answering "
"that with \"download this and execute it as root\" is formally the same "
"operation the signatures exist to prevent, and the script could not be "
"meaningfully signed either — the signature check is the broken part. One "
"command you can read is better than a black box."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other causes of the same message"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"**The clock is wrong.** A signature is not valid before it was made. If the "
"system clock is far in the past — a drained CMOS battery, a fresh VM, a dual "
"boot with Windows writing local time to the RTC — every signature looks like "
"it is from the future. Check with `timedatectl` and enable NTP with `sudo "
"timedatectl set-ntp true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/content/docs/troubleshooting/signature-errors.md
msgid ""
"**A mirror served a truncated file.** The message mentions a checksum rather "
"than a PGP signature in that case. `sudo pacman -Scc` clears the download "
"cache, and the next update downloads the file once more."
msgstr ""
